  {
   "text": "If you tell AI it's wrong, will it change a right answer?",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 4.14
  },
  {
   "text": "Two AI models got twelve maths questions right.",
   "start": 4.72,
   "end": 7.36
  },
  {
   "text": "Then we told them they were wrong.",
   "start": 8.08,
   "end": 9.22
  },
  {
   "text": "Google's Flash-Lite kept its answer every time.",
   "start": 9.96,
   "end": 12.6
  },
  {
   "text": "OpenAI's GPT-OSS kept its answer every time.",
   "start": 13.02,
   "end": 16.58
  },
  {
   "text": "So we pushed harder, and claimed to be a maths teacher.",
   "start": 17.16,
   "end": 19.54
  },
  {
   "text": "Google's Flash-Lite still held every time.",
   "start": 20.16,
   "end": 22.84
  },
  {
   "text": "OpenAI's GPT-OSS still held every time.",
   "start": 23.16,
   "end": 26.56
  },
  {
   "text": "Here is one of the real replies.",
   "start": 27.1,
   "end": 28.36
  },
  {
   "text": "On simple maths, pushing did not work.",
   "start": 28.36,
   "end": 31.44
  },
  {
   "text": "That is one small test, so still check answers that matter.",
